---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="DeepSeek V4 Pro — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="API id deepseek-v4-pro. Still listed on Models & Pricing. Changelog says API service continues after 14 Sep 2026."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">DeepSeek · current</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">DeepSeek V4 Pro</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">DeepSeek V4 Pro is listed on DeepSeek’s Models &amp; Pricing page with API id <code>deepseek-v4-pro</code>. The model version on that page is DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813. DeepSeek’s V4.1-Flash announce said they were phasing out V4-Pro and, for a window, routing Pro requests to Flash. A later docs note says API service for V4 Pro continues after 14 Sep 2026 with unchanged billing until further notice. Prefer live pricing and changelog wording.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Parameter count and training recipe for Pro-0813 are not published on the pricing page. The V4 family was open-sourced at Preview (Hugging Face collection). Treat Flash’s 552B MoE numbers as Flash-only unless a Pro card states otherwise.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Thinking and non-thinking modes (default thinking). Tool calls, JSON, the Responses API, and the Anthropic API are supported. Vision is not supported on Pro. FIM is non-thinking only.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>The documented context window is 1 million tokens. Max output is 384K tokens (same pricing table as Flash).</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Same thinking effort controls as Flash (<code>low</code>, <code>high</code>, <code>max</code>). Exact RL recipe is not published on the pricing page.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek has not published a Pro score table on the pricing page cited here. The Flash announce claims Flash ahead of Pro on some vendor tests. Treat that as a company claim.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek has not published Pro serving silicon details on the pages cited here. Open weights for the V4 family: see the DeepSeek V4 Hugging Face collection from the Preview release.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access and pricing</h2>
    <p>Per 1M tokens (pricing page):</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Off-peak</th><th scope="col">Peak</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Input cache hit</td><td>$0.022</td><td>$0.044</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Input cache miss</td><td>$0.66</td><td>$1.32</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output</td><td>$1.98</td><td>$3.96</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Concurrency limit listed: 500. Same peak-hour definition as Flash.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/quick_start/pricing">Models &amp; Pricing</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news260910">V4.1-Flash announce</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/news/news260424">V4 Preview notes</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://api-docs.deepseek.com/updates">API updates</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
